    "http://schema.org/givenName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Yotam"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/familyName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Haber"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>2020 Azrieli Commission for Jewish Music Laureate</p><p>Yotam Haber was born in the Netherlands and grew up in Israel, Nigeria, and Milwaukee. He is the recipient of numerous prestigious awards, residencies, and commissions, and his compositions are frequently performed by the world’s leading contemporary music ensembles. Haber is an Associate Professor at the Conservatory of the University of Missouri-Kansas City and Artistic Director Emeritus of MATA, the non-profit organization founded by Philip Glass, which since 1996 has commissioned and presented new works by young composers from around the world.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
